  "worked_solution": "Our quantified statement reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $n\\in N$ **such that**, **for all** $m\\in Z,\\,nm$ is divisible by $2.$\n\nThis can be re-phrased as follows:\n\n$\\,$ There exists a natural number $n$ such that the product of $n$ and any integer $m$ is divisible by $2.$",
